# AI Rules for Apex Naming Conventions

## NC-001: General Salesforce Component Naming

**Scope**: All Salesforce components unless specific rules override

**Core Requirements**:
- Use `UpperCamelCase` for all component names
- **NEVER** use underscores in names (except Test and BatchJob classes)
- **NEVER** replace spaces with underscores
- Always treat names as case-sensitive
- If component has separate label, make it same as name but with spaces
- If component has separate label, make it same as name but with spaces
- Always populate Description/Help Text fields

**Examples**:
```
✅ MyEmailTemplate (Name) → "My Email Template" (Label)
✅ CaseTaggingTool
✅ MessageViewer
❌ My_Email_Template
❌ case_tagging_tool
```

---

## NC-002: Apex Class Naming Patterns

**Scope**: All Apex classes

**Naming Patterns**:

| Class Type | Pattern | Example | Notes |
|------------|---------|---------|-------|
| Batch | `BatchJob_<Name>` | `BatchJob_Account` | Only exception to underscore rule |
| Data Access | `<ObjectName>Selector` | `AccountSelector` | Remove `__c` from custom objects |
| Domain/Trigger | `<ObjectName>TriggerHelper` | `AccountTriggerHelper` | Remove `__c` from custom objects |
| Helper | `<ObjectName>Helper` or `<Type>Helper` | `AccountHelper`, `StringHelper` | |
| REST API | `<ResourceName>RestAPI` | `ContractRestAPI` | |
| Scheduler | `<Name>Scheduler` | `ChurnSurveyScheduler` | |
| Service | `<ResourceName>Svc` | `LocationSvc`, `QuoteSvc` | |
| Unit Test | `Test_<ClassName>` | `Test_AccountHelper` | Only exception to underscore rule |
| VF Controller | `<PageName>Ctrl` | `MessageViewerCtrl` | |

**Custom Object Reference**: Use object name without `__c` suffix in class names.

---

## NC-003: Class Member Naming Standards

**Scope**: All Apex class members

**Member Naming**:

| Member Type | Pattern | Example | Notes |
|-------------|---------|---------|-------|
| Constants | `UPPER_UNDERSCORE` | `private final Integer MAX_QUERY_LIMIT = 100;` | For anything marked `final` |
| Fields/Properties | `lowerCamelCase` | `public String name;` | All visibility levels |
| Boolean Fields | `is/has + CamelCase` | `public Boolean isSomething;` | Start with `is` or `has` |
| Methods | `lowerCamelCase` | `public void myMethod();` | All visibility levels |
| Parameters | `lowerCamelCase` | `public void myMethod(String myParam)` | |
| Local Variables | `lowerCamelCase` | `Integer intVar = 20;` | |
| Nested Classes | `UpperCamelCase` | `class MyNestedClass {}` | |
| Interfaces | `I + UpperCamelCase` | `interface IMyInterface {}` | Always prefix with `I` |
| Enums | Name: `UpperCamelCase`, Values: `UPPER_UNDERSCORE` | `enum Season { SUMMER, WINTER }` | |

**Map Naming**:
- Use "to" preposition: `accNameToApprovalMap`
- For same object key/value: `accsMap` 
- ❌ Avoid "By" preposition: `approvalByAccNameMap`

