## NC-004: Custom Field Naming Rules

**Scope**: All Salesforce custom fields

**General Rule**: Use `UpperCamelCase` with no underscores

**Field-Specific Patterns**:

| Field Type | Pattern | Example | Label Example |
|------------|---------|---------|---------------|
| Checkbox | `Is<Name>__c` or `Has<Name>__c` | `IsActive__c` | "Active" |
| Lookup/Master-Detail | `<ObjectName>__c` | `MyCustomObject__c` | "My Custom Object" |

**Requirements**:
- Checkbox labels can drop "Is" prefix for readability
- Child relationship names must be descriptive
- Always use meaningful, descriptive names

**Examples**:
```
✅ IsActive__c → Label: "Active"
✅ HasLineItems__c → Label: "Has Line Items"  
✅ MyCustomObject__c → Label: "My Custom Object"
❌ Is_Active__c
❌ my_custom_object__c
```

---

## NC-005: Trigger and Component Naming

**Scope**: Apex Triggers, Lightning Components, Visualforce

**Trigger Naming**:
- Pattern: `<ObjectName>.trigger`
- Examples: `Account.trigger`, `MyCustomObject.trigger`
- **NEVER** include "Trigger" suffix in name
- **NEVER** include `__c` suffix for custom objects

**Component Naming**:

| Component Type | Pattern | Example | Notes |
|----------------|---------|---------|-------|
| Custom Object | `UpperCamelCase` | `MyCustomObject__c` | Salesforce adds suffix automatically |
| Visualforce Component | `UpperCamelCase` | `LearningCenterFooter` | |
| Visualforce Page | `UpperCamelCase` | `MessageViewer` | |
| Lightning Component | `UpperCamelCase` | `CaseTaggingTool` | |
| Lightning Web Component | `UpperCamelCase` | `scAdminHeader` | Use unmanaged prefix |

---

## NC-006: Custom Label Standards

**Scope**: All Salesforce custom labels

**Requirements**:
- Use `UpperCamelCase` with no underscores
- Always populate `category` field to show usage location
- Always populate description field

**Examples**:
```
✅ Name: MyEmailTemplateTitle
   Category: EmailTemplates
   Description: Title text for account email template

✅ Name: CaseTaggingHeader  
   Category: LightningComponents.CaseTagging
   Description: Header text for case tagging component

❌ My_Email_Template_Title
❌ Missing category or description
```

## NC-007: Best Practices

**Scope**: All Salesforce components

**Best Practices**:
- Group related labels with consistent category naming
- Use descriptive categories like "ComponentName.FeatureName"
- Make descriptions specific enough for other developers to understand usage

